---
/**
 * The legal notice French law asks of every website (mentions légales) and
 * what the site does with a visit: the publisher, the host, what the browser
 * keeps, what the host processes, the licenses and the credits. Each
 * statement must stay true of the site's code and of its Cloudflare zone:
 * no cookie, no analytics, nothing loaded from another site.
 */
import SiteFooter from '../components/landing/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/landing/SiteHeader.astro';
import Landing from '../layouts/Landing.astro';
import { describedVersion, docsSource } from '../lib/docs-source';
import { LEGAL_UPDATED, LICENSE_URL, REPO_URL } from '../lib/site';
---

<Landing
  title="Legal notice and privacy | Spawner"
  description="Who publishes and hosts spawner.run, and what happens to your visit: no cookies, no analytics, nothing loaded from another site."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="legal-title">
      <div class="wrap text">
        <div class="part">
          <h1 class="section-title" id="legal-title">Legal notice and privacy</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Who publishes spawner.run, who hosts it, and what happens when you visit it: no cookies, no analytics, nothing loaded from another site.
          </p>
          <p class="updated">Updated on <time datetime={LEGAL_UPDATED.iso}>{LEGAL_UPDATED.text}</time>.</p>
        </div>

        <section class="part" aria-labelledby="mentions-legales">
          <h2 id="mentions-legales" lang="fr">Mentions légales</h2>
          <p>What French law asks every website to state: who publishes it, how to reach them, and who hosts it.</p>
          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>Publisher</dt>
              <dd>
                The maintainer of Spawner, <a href="https://github.com/Flosk6">Flosk6</a> on GitHub: a private individual who publishes this site on a
                non-professional basis. As article 1-1, II of the French law of 21 June 2004 on confidence in the digital economy
                (<span lang="fr">loi pour la confiance dans l’économie numérique</span>, LCEN) allows, the publisher’s name and address are not shown
                here: the publisher gave them to the host, as that article requires.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Contact</dt>
              <dd>
                Through GitHub: <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`}>an issue</a> for a question about this site or Spawner, or
                <a href={`${REPO_URL}/security/advisories/new`}>a private report</a> for a security vulnerability, as the
                <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/master/SECURITY.md`}>security policy</a> describes.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Host</dt>
              <dd>
                Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, United States. Phone: +1 (650) 319-8930.
                <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/">cloudflare.com</a>
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <section class="part" aria-labelledby="privacy">
          <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            This site sets no cookies and runs no analytics or tracking script. It loads nothing from another site: its fonts, images and search index
            are files of spawner.run. Links to GitHub, npm and other sites take you there only when you follow them.
          </p>

          <h3 id="what-your-browser-keeps">What your browser keeps</h3>
          <p>
            Two settings, which stay on your device and are sent to no one: the theme you pick, light or dark, in the browser’s local storage (under
            the key <code>starlight-theme</code>); and on documentation pages, which groups of the sidebar are open and where it is scrolled, in its
            session storage, which the browser empties when you close the tab. Clearing this site’s data in your browser removes both.
          </p>

          <h3 id="what-the-host-processes">What the host processes</h3>
          <p>
            To deliver each page and protect the site from attacks, Cloudflare handles the technical data of every request: the IP address it comes
            from, the address asked for, the browser’s user agent and the time. It does so on the publisher’s behalf, and keeps this data as
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">its privacy policy</a> describes; for data that leaves the European Union, Cloudflare
            is certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework. The publisher keeps no logs of its own and does not combine this data with any
            other. This processing rests on the publisher’s legitimate interest in serving the site and keeping it secure (article 6(1)(f) of the
            GDPR).
          </p>

          <h3 id="your-rights">Your rights</h3>
          <p>
            Under the GDPR, you can ask for access to the data about you or for its erasure, and object to its processing, through the contact above;
            beyond what Cloudflare processes, the publisher holds none. You can also lodge a complaint with the CNIL, the French data protection
            authority (<a href="https://www.cnil.fr/">cnil.fr</a>).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="part" aria-labelledby="licenses">
          <h2 id="licenses">Licenses and credits</h2>
          <p>
            Spawner is free and open source, under the <a href={LICENSE_URL}>Apache License 2.0</a>. The documentation and the changelog of this site
            come from its repository and share its license, and the code of the site itself is under the same license, in
            <a href="https://github.com/Flosk6/spawner-site">Flosk6/spawner-site</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            The site is built with <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a>, <a href="https://starlight.astro.build/">Starlight</a> and
            <a href="https://pagefind.app/">Pagefind</a>, under the MIT license. Its typefaces, served from the site itself, are Overpass and Overpass
            Mono, by the Overpass Project Authors, and Chakra Petch, by the Chakra Petch Project Authors, under the
            <a href="https://openfontlicense.org/">SIL Open Font License 1.1</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter described={describedVersion(docsSource())} />
</Landing>

<style>
  .text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3.5rem;
  }

  .part {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .lede {
    color: var(--sp-text-2);
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
  }

  .updated {
    color: var(--sp-text-3);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.625rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  h3 {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  p,
  dd {
    color: var(--sp-text-2);
  }

  dl {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sp-border);
  }

  dl > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.25rem 2rem;
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sp-border);
  }

  dt {
    color: var(--sp-text);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    dl > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
